# 3L Moto UI Design Rules

Source guidance adapted from [PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules) (Next.js + React + Tailwind + shadcn) plus project taste constraints.

## Design Read (always)
Reading this as: redesign of an **operational rental admin** for shop staff, with a **Linear/Notion-clean** language, density medium, single cobalt accent. Not a marketing landing page.

## Stack (do not invent alternatives)
- Next.js App Router, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, Supabase
- Shared shell: `components/dashboard/module-shell.tsx`, `rental-ui.tsx`
- Tokens: `app/globals.css` (`.text-display|title|body|label|meta`, `.money`, radius/shadow vars)
- Font: Be Vietnam Pro via `next/font` in `app/layout.tsx`

## Visual language
- Background: cool slate (`--background`), surfaces white, one border `slate-200`
- Accent: cobalt blue only for CTA / active nav / focus
- Semantic: emerald = income/positive, amber = warning, rose = overdue/destructive
- Radius: container 16px, control 12px, badge 8px — use CSS vars
- Shadows: tinted slate, low opacity — no multi-layer glow, no purple gradients
- No Inter/Roboto as primary; no emoji in UI chrome; no ALL-CAPS italic brand headers

## Typography (mandatory scale)
Use utilities, do not invent one-off sizes:
- `.text-display` — page titles
- `.text-title` — section / card titles
- `.text-body` — content (≥15px; inputs ≥16px on mobile)
- `.text-label` — form labels / table heads
- `.text-meta` — captions (never below 12px)
- `.money` — tabular figures for VND

## Layout & components
- Compose pages with `ModulePageShell`, `ModuleBrandHeader` / `ModuleSubpageHeader`, `ModuleKpiGrid`, `ModuleSectionCard`, `ModuleToolbar`, `ModuleEmptyState`, `ModuleResponsiveTable`, `ModulePagination`
- KPI hierarchy: label → value → sublabel; same height in a row
- Desktop table + mobile cards via `ModuleResponsiveTable`
- Touch targets ≥44px; primary actions `h-11`
- Prefer shell primitives over page-local card/filter styles

## Code quality (from awesome-cursorrules)
- Functional components; descriptive names (`isLoading`, `hasError`)
- Mobile-first Tailwind; loading / empty / error states for every list
- Keep client boundaries small; do not rewrite business logic during UI work
- Never `@apply` custom utilities like `text-label` inside CSS (Tailwind v4 build break)

## Anti-patterns
- Mixing `gray-*` and `slate-*` arbitrarily — prefer slate
- Hardcoded `text-xs` / `text-[15px]` / rainbow accents per page
- DaisyUI / Biome / forcing `/src` relocation (not this project's stack)
- Dark mode / glassmorphism / AI-purple themes
